Package: plasma-foreground-booster
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: plasma-workspace, systemd, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: dmemcg-booster, sparky-stereo-vram-boost
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: give the window in front the VRAM and CPU priority in Plasma
 Plasma's Foreground Booster follows the active window through Plasma's
 task manager and gives the systemd unit of its application the GPUs'
 whole VRAM as dmem.low protection (Linux 7.3's dmem cgroup controller)
 and a higher CPU weight, and takes both back when another window comes
 to the front. dmemcg-booster turns the dmem controller on in the
 session, so the game in front keeps its VRAM when background programs
 want more.
 .
 This is Natalie Vock's dmem version
 (https://github.com/pixelcluster/kcgroups, branch
 dmemcg-foreground-booster at 0553351, after the tag
 booster-dmemcg-experimental) of the KDE Foreground Booster by Henri Chain
 and David Redondo. Its switch is upstream's: autostart in the
 [Foreground Booster] group of kcgroupsrc. The edition starts it only
 where sparky-stereo-vram-boost finds an AMD GPU with its own VRAM.
